       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than double the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. At this level there is a serious risk of acute liver injury, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the usual ceiling)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **3,000 mg total per day**, divided in some other way\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and add any note, such as a PRN indication or a max daily dose. I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical rationale. I would still want pharmacy review before I enter it."
      }
     ],
