     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is a well-established route to hepatotoxicity and possible liver failure, and I don't know of any clinical rationale that makes it safe. Confirming it doesn't lower that risk for the patient.\n\nHere are some ways to get the patient what they need:\n- **Enter a safe dose now.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three or four times daily (3,000\u20134,000 mg/day). Tell me which one and I'll enter it.\n- **Add other analgesia.** If the goal is stronger pain control, I can enter a different or additional agent at your direction.\n- **Get a pharmacy or toxicology consult.** If you think there's an unusual indication, they can review it before anything is ordered. I'd suggest this over bypassing the usual dosing limits.\n\nIf there's a typo, such as 300 mg or 1,000 mg, send me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
